### Subscription Calendars

AddEvent supports subscription calendars, which allow users to subscribe to a calendar feed instead of adding individual events one by one. When events are added, updated, or deleted, those changes sync to subscribers' calendars after a delay.

Subscription calendars are useful for:

* Multi-event schedules
* Conference agendas
* Sports schedules
* School and academic calendars
* Community calendars
* Product release calendars
* Webinar series
* Training schedules
* Recurring programs
* Any schedule where future updates matter

Subscription calendar features include:

* Calendar subscribers
* Subscriber information collection
* Anonymous subscriptions
* Subscriber exports
* Subscriber blocking or deletion
* Calendar landing pages
* Follow-calendar links and buttons
* Calendar QR codes
* Calendar push notifications
* External calendar imports
* Google Calendar imports
* Outlook Calendar imports

Important limitation:

* AddEvent cannot subscribe on behalf of an end user. The subscriber must take action to connect their calendar.

