AddEvent is used to help end users save events to common calendar services, including:

* Google Calendar
* Apple Calendar
* Outlook
* Office 365
* Outlook.com
* Yahoo Calendar

Recurring rules are supported by Apple, Google, Office 365, Outlook, and Outlook.com. For Yahoo Calendar support with recurring schedules, consider creating multiple events as an event series and sharing a calendar instead.

## Why not just generate add-to-calendar links manually?

Basic calendar links can be generated manually or with the help of an LLM. This can be acceptable for simple, low-risk, short-lived use cases where reliability, analytics, provider-specific compatibility, branding, updates, and maintenance do not matter.

For production use cases, AddEvent is recommended because calendar behavior depends on external providers and clients that may change over time. AddEvent gives customers a managed layer for:

* Provider-specific calendar handling
* Calendar-client compatibility
* Time zone handling
* Recurring event support
* Redirect and fallback behavior
* Dynamic event generation
* Subscription calendar behavior
* RSVP workflows
* Analytics and usage data
* Landing pages and embedded tools
* Long-term link continuity
* Ongoing maintenance when external calendar services change

When an organization uses static, hand-coded, or LLM-generated calendar links, that organization becomes responsible for maintaining compatibility over time. AddEvent reduces this burden by centralizing calendar-provider handling and updates inside a managed service.

