## Product glossary

* Event: A single calendar item created and shared through AddEvent.
* RSVP Event: An event with registration and attendee collection enabled.
* Calendar: A container for events inside AddEvent.
* Subscription Calendar: A dynamic calendar feed that users can subscribe to so updates sync to their calendars.
* Calendar Subscriber: A user who has subscribed to a calendar.
* Add to Calendar Link: A link that allows a user to save an event to a calendar.
* Add to Calendar Button: A button that allows a user to save an event to a calendar.
* Follow Calendar Link: A link that allows a user to subscribe to a calendar.
* Follow Calendar Button: A button that allows a user to subscribe to a calendar.
* Event Landing Page: A public page for a single event.
* Calendar Landing Page: A public page for a calendar or event schedule.
* Embeddable Calendar: A calendar experience embedded on a website.
* Embeddable Events List: A list of events embedded on a website.
* Dynamic Add to Calendar: A feature for generating personalized calendar invites dynamically from user-specific or system-generated event data.
* RSVP Form: A reusable form for collecting event registration information.
* Design Template: A reusable no-code design for landing pages, embedded calendars, or emails.
* Notification Flow: A configurable RSVP email notification workflow.
* Merge Tag: A placeholder used to personalize RSVP and notification emails.
* API Token: A token used to authenticate API requests.

